{"step_index":6042,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T11:14:41Z","thinking":"The `.mp4` string absence in the temporary journal is unexpected. The file system's filename storage method could be a factor. The `data.find(b'.mp4')` returning 0 needs further investigation. The database was located in a different directory than initially assumed. Awaiting clarification on where `output_packaged` resides.\n\n\nThe recovered MP4s originated from `MAGIC-2`, carved from unallocated inodes on the NVMe drive `/dev/nvme1n1`. The initial count of 136 videos raises the question of where the remaining videos are located, prompting investigation of other video formats and the potentially misidentified `.unknown` files. The header bytes `ftyp` (at offset 4) will be used to identify video file headers directly within `/dev/nvme1n1`'s unallocated sectors, and thus find the other videos. A python script will be crafted to scan the raw device for these headers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"sudo python3 -c \\\"\\nimport struct, os\\n\\nprint('Scanning /dev/nvme1n1 for MP4/video ftyp headers...')\\nCHUNK_SIZE = 16 * 1024 * 1024 # 16 MB\\n\\nvalid_brands = [b'isom', b'iso2', b'mp41', b'mp42', b'avc1', b'qt  ', b'M4V ', b'MSNV']\\n\\ntotal_found = 0\\nfound_offsets = []\\n\\n# Scan first 50 GB of disk or sample\\nwith open('/dev/nvme1n1', 'rb') as dev:\\n    offset = 0\\n    # Let's scan up to 100 GB (or 6000 chunks of 16MB)\\n    for i in range(2000): # 32 GB\\n        chunk = dev.read(CHUNK_SIZE)\\n        if not chunk:\\n            break\\n        pos = 0\\n        while True:\\n            pos = chunk.find(b'ftyp', pos)\\n            if pos == -1:\\n                break\\n            if pos >= 4:\\n                brand = chunk[pos+4:pos+8]\\n                if brand in valid_brands:\\n                    # check box size\\n                    box_sz = struct.unpack('>I', chunk[pos-4:pos])[0]\\n                    if 16 <= box_sz <= 1024:\\n                        abs_pos = offset + pos - 4\\n                        found_offsets.append((abs_pos, brand))\\n                        total_found += 1\\n            pos += 4\\n        offset += len(chunk)\\n        if (i + 1) % 500 == 0:\\n            print(f'Scanned {(offset)/1024/1024/1024:.1f} GB... Found {total_found} MP4 headers so far')\\n\\nprint(f'Done 32 GB scan! Total MP4 headers found: {total_found}')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"8000","toolAction":"\"Scanning raw NVMe drive for all MP4 headers\"","toolSummary":"\"Scan raw NVMe drive for all MP4 headers\""}}]}
{"step_index":6043,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-25T11:14:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T11:14:48Z\nTool is running as a background task with task id: 47f3f05e-b686-4d3d-9ae2-f215c03ab86b/task-6043\nTask Description: sudo python3 -c \"\nimport struct, os\n\nprint('Scanning /dev/nvme1n1 for MP4/video ftyp headers...')\nCHUNK_SIZE = 16 * 1024 * 1024 # 16 MB\n\nvalid_brands = [b'isom', b'iso2', b'mp41', b'mp42', b'avc1', b'qt  ', b'M4V ', b'MSNV']\n\ntotal_found = 0\nfound_offsets = []\n\n# Scan first 50 GB of disk or sample\nwith open('/dev/nvme1n1', 'rb') as dev:\n    offset = 0\n    # Let's scan up to 100 GB (or 6000 chunks of 16MB)\n    for i in range(2000): # 32 GB\n        chunk = dev.read(CHUNK_SIZE)\n        if not chunk:\n            break\n        pos = 0\n        while True:\n            pos = chunk.find(b'ftyp', pos)\n            if pos == -1:\n                break\n            if pos >= 4:\n                brand = chunk[pos+4:pos+8]\n                if brand in valid_brands:\n                    # check box size\n                    box_sz = struct.unpack('>I', chunk[pos-4:pos])[0]\n                    if 16 <= box_sz <= 1024:\n                        abs_pos = offset + pos - 4\n                        found_offsets.append((abs_pos, brand))\n                        total_found += 1\n            pos += 4\n        offset += len(chunk)\n        if (i + 1) % 500 == 0:\n            print(f'Scanned {(offset)/1024/1024/1024:.1f} GB... Found {total_found} MP4 headers so far')\n\nprint(f'Done 32 GB scan! Total MP4 headers found: {total_found}')\n\"\nTask logs are available at: file:///home/azureuser/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/47f3f05e-b686-4d3d-9ae2-f215c03ab86b/.system_generated/tasks/task-6043.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to fin